#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.cedarloom"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom <command> [options]\n"
"cloom is a short name for cedarloom.\n"
"\n"
"Commands:\n"
"  doctor           Check that this computer and project can run CedarLoom.\n"
"  runs list        List the runs recorded for this project.\n"
"  runs show <run>  Show a run and its steps.\n"
"  undo <run>       Undo a run, as a run of its own.\n"
"  workflows list   List the shipped and project workflow definitions.\n"
"  workflows show <name>\n"
"                   Show a workflow definition.\n"
"  workflows validate [<name>...]\n"
"                   Check workflow definitions with the plugin's generator.\n"
"  workflows generate [<name>...]\n"
"                   Write the files of workflow definitions into .claude.\n"
"\n"
"Options:\n"
"  --json           Print one JSON document instead of text.\n"
"  --help, -h       Show the usage of a command.\n"
"  --version, -V    Print the version of CedarLoom."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.runs"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom runs <verb> [options]\n"
"\n"
"Verbs:\n"
"  list        List the runs recorded for this project, newest first.\n"
"  show <run>  Show a run and its steps."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.doctor"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom doctor [--plugin-root <dir>] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"Checks that this computer can run CedarLoom: the Node.js version, the project,\n"
"the cl-workflow plugin from the CedarLoom marketplace: installed for this\n"
"project, new enough and enabled, and the workflow definitions in\n"
".cedarloom/workflows: valid, and their generated files in .claude up to date.\n"
"For the definitions it runs the plugin's generator in a temporary folder.\n"
"\n"
"Options:\n"
"  --plugin-root <dir>  Use this cl-workflow folder instead of the installed\n"
"                       plugin, and run its generator. Its origin is not\n"
"                       checked."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.workflows"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom workflows <verb> [options]\n"
"\n"
"Verbs:\n"
"  list                List the shipped and project workflow definitions.\n"
"  show <name>         Show a workflow definition.\n"
"  validate [<name>...]\n"
"                      Check workflow definitions with the plugin's generator.\n"
"  generate [<name>...]\n"
"                      Write the files of workflow definitions into .claude."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.workflows-list"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom workflows list [--plugin-root <dir>] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"Lists the workflow definitions shipped with the cl-workflow plugin, which are\n"
"read only, and the project's own in .cedarloom/workflows. Without a usable\n"
"plugin it lists the project's alone.\n"
"\n"
"Options:\n"
"  --plugin-root <dir>  Use this cl-workflow folder instead of the installed\n"
"                       plugin. Its origin is not checked."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.workflows-show"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom workflows show <name> [--shipped] [--plugin-root <dir>] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"Shows the project's workflow definition <name>: each stage and phase by its\n"
"JSON Pointer, then the definition.\n"
"\n"
"Options:\n"
"  --shipped            Show the definition shipped with the plugin.\n"
"  --plugin-root <dir>  Use this cl-workflow folder instead of the installed\n"
"                       plugin. Its origin is not checked."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.workflows-validate"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom workflows validate [<name>...] [--shipped] [--plugin-root <dir>] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"Checks the project's workflow definitions <name>, or all of them, with the\n"
"plugin's generator, run in a temporary folder, and prints each problem's file,\n"
"field and rule. Exits 1 when a definition has a problem.\n"
"\n"
"Options:\n"
"  --shipped            Check the definitions shipped with the plugin.\n"
"  --plugin-root <dir>  Use this cl-workflow folder instead of the installed\n"
"                       plugin, and run its generator. Its origin is not\n"
"                       checked."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.workflows-generate"
msgstr ""
"Usage: cedarloom workflows generate [<name>...] [--yes] [--plugin-root <dir>] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"Generates the project's workflow definitions <name>, or all of them, with the\n"
"plugin's generator, run in a temporary folder, and plans the changes to\n"
".claude: the files to create or replace, and the files an earlier generation\n"
"wrote that are no longer generated, deleted only while unchanged. Without --yes\n"
"it shows the plan and does not apply it. Undo a generation with cedarloom undo.\n"
"\n"
"Options:\n"
"  --yes                Apply the plan as a run.\n"
"  --plugin-root <dir>  Use this cl-workflow folder instead of the installed\n"
"                       plugin, and run its generator. Its origin is not\n"
"                       checked."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.runs-list"
msgstr "Usage: cedarloom runs list [--json]\n\nLists the runs recorded for this project, newest first."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.runs-show"
msgstr "Usage: cedarloom runs show <run> [--json]\n\nShows the run <run> and its steps."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "help.undo"
msgstr "Usage: cedarloom undo <run> [--yes] [--json]\n\nUndoes the run <run> as a run of its own. Without --yes it shows the plan and does not apply it."

